p:
Express as a common fraction in simplest form: $$
\sqrt{7\frac{9}{16}}
$$

s:
Let $O$ be the origin, and let $P,$ $Q,$ $V$ be the points corresponding to vectors $\mathbf{p},$ $\mathbf{q},$ and $\mathbf{v},$ respectively. Then $\frac{OP}{OV} = \frac{3}{4}.$

[asy]
import olympiad;
unitsize (0.5 cm);

pair O, P, Q, V;

O = (0,0);
P = (3,0);
V = (4,5);
Q = (P + reflect(O,V)*(P))/2;

draw(O--P--V--cycle);
draw(P--Q);
draw(rightanglemark(O,P,V,14));
draw(rightanglemark(P,Q,O,14));

label("$O$", O, SW);
label("$P$", P, SE);
label("$Q$", Q, NW);
label("$V$", V, NE);
[/asy]

Because right triangles $OQP$ and $OPV$ are similar (both are right triangles and $\angle OPV = \angle OQP$ as $\mathbf{q}$ is the projection of $\mathbf{p}$ onto $\mathbf{v}$),
\[\frac{OQ}{OP} = \frac{OP}{OV} = \frac{3}{4}.\]
Thus, using the property of similar triangles:
\[\frac{\|\mathbf{q}\|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|} = \frac{OQ}{OV} = \left(\frac{OQ}{OP}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{OP}{OV}\right) = \left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2 = \boxed{\frac{9}{16}}.\]

Let \( x = 7.2\overline{34} \). To eliminate the repeating decimal, consider \( 100x = 734.\overline{34} \).

Setting up the equation:
$$
\begin{align*}
100x &= 734.\overline{34} \\
x &= 7.2\overline{34}
\end{align*}
$$

Subtract the second equation from the first:
$$
\begin{align*}
100x - x &= 734.\overline{34} - 7.2\overline{34} \\
99x &= 727.14 \\
x &= \frac{727.14}{99}
\end{align*}
$$

This fraction can be simplified by noting that the denominator should factor out the influence of the repeating decimal:
$$
x = \frac{727.14}{99} = \frac{72714}{9900}
$$

Upon simplification,
$$
x = \frac{36357}{4950}
$$

Therefore, \( 7.2\overline{34} = \boxed{\frac{36357}{4950}} \).

